# GanttChartEditor → SchedulerWeb: "計画管理ツールへ送信" integration

## Context

GanttChartEditor and SchedulerWeb are two independent apps (sibling folders under `web/`) that currently know nothing about each other. GanttChartEditor already has a toolbar button "▶ 計画管理ツールへ送信" that is a pure stub — clicking it just shows "not implemented yet" (`Toolbar.tsx:70`). This was anticipated in GanttChartEditor's own roadmap as "Phase 5: Connect GanttChart ↔ Scheduler Webapp — Submit → opens Webapp New Run" (`documents/GanttChartEditor_implementation_plan20260618.md`), and there's even a pre-placed `SERVICE_BASE_URL` constant waiting for it (`appConfig.ts:17`).

The goal of this task (first of two planned directions — Gantt→Scheduler now, Scheduler→Gantt later) is: clicking the button confirms, saves both YAML files (same format as the existing Save feature), sends them to SchedulerWeb, and opens SchedulerWeb with its "新規実行" (new run) dialog already showing both files attached — auto-launching SchedulerWeb (frontend + its `web/service` backend) in the background if it isn't already running. The user reviews and clicks the actual submit button in SchedulerWeb themselves (no auto-submit).

## End-to-end flow

```
Click "計画管理ツールへ送信" → confirm dialog → confirm
  1. Save both YAMLs to Downloads (existing downloadBothYamlFiles, unchanged)
  2. POST /api/handoff/create {envYaml, scheduleYaml} → GanttChartEditor's own server (:3010)
       - stores payload in an in-memory Map<token, payload> (5 min TTL)
       - health-checks SchedulerWeb frontend (:5174) and web/service (:3001 GET /queue)
       - if either is down: spawns `npm run dev:all` in SchedulerWeb's folder (detached, unref'd)
       - polls both up to ~28s
       - responds { ok, url: 'http://localhost:5174/?incomingTransfer=<token>' } or an error
  3. window.open(url) → SchedulerWeb tab
  4. SchedulerWeb (RunLogPage) sees ?incomingTransfer=<token> on mount
       - GET http://localhost:3010/api/handoff/consume/<token> (cross-origin, one-time use)
       - builds two File objects from the returned YAML strings
       - opens NewRunModal pre-filled with both files (no auto-submit)
       - strips the query param from the URL
```

